{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960716,"nonce":"LeLRtQJGdDgv7cloMW3vXzBfPFI=","title":"the Haxe surface loads xidl.hdll but the release ships xgpu.hdll","message":"Since 3b2047c the generated Haxe asks for `@:hlNative(\"xidl\", ...)` (589 primitives in haxe/gpu), so HashLink and Ash look for `xidl.hdll` natively and `xidl.wasm` in a page. The release still names the library `xgpu.hdll` (.github/workflows/release.yml) and `xgpu.wasm` (scripts/build_wasm.sh), and build_wasm.sh and release.yml collect exports with `sed ... @:hlNative(\"xgpu\", ...)`, which now matches nothing: the wasm job stops at \"no xgpu primitives found in haxe/gpu\". docs/using.md still says xgpu.hdll.\n\nx-idl can now name the library: `x_idl::Library(\"xgpu\")` (or any name) for both the model and the Haxe surface. Pick one name and use it in the generator call, the release names and the export scan.","files":null}]}